"computer\" with no initiative, then you would have to spell out a full description of how the game would be played in every contingency.\n\u2022 For example, in chess, this would be an impossible task (though in some simpler games, it can be done).\n\u2022 Thinking in terms of strategies is important.\n\u2022 But in strategic form games, there is no difference between an action and a pure strategy, and we will use them interchangeably."]}, "id": "BB_2", "from_name": "transcription", "to_name": "image", "type": "textarea", "origin": "prediction"}, {"original_width": 1920, "original_height": 1080, "image_rotation": 0, "value": {"x": 34.97121710526316, "y": 0.1644736842105263, "width": 28.495065789473678, "height": 2.4671052631578947, "rotation": 0}, "id": "XBWwF6w02e", "from_name": "bbox", "to_name": "image", "type": "rectangle", "origin": "manual"}, {"original_width": 1920, "original_height": 1080, "image_rotation": 0, "value": {"x": 34.97121710526316, "y": 0.1644736842105263, "width": 28.495065789473678, "height": 2.4671052631578947, "rotation": 0, "labels": ["text"]}, "id": "XBWwF6w02e", "from_name": "label", "to_name": "image", "type": "labels", "origin": "manual"}, {"original_width": 1920, "original_height": 1080, "image_rotation": 0, "value": {"x": 34.97121710526316, "y": 0.1644736842105263, "width": 28.495065789473678, "height": 2.4671052631578947, "rotation": 0, "text": ["Game Theory: Lecture 2 Strategic Form Games"]}, "id": "XBWwF6w02e", "from_name": "transcription", "to_name": "image", "type": "textarea", "origin": "manual"}], "created_username": "10. NAIST nlp_annot_10@naist.ac.jp, 16", "created_ago": "0\u00a0minutes", "completed_by": {"id": 16, "first_name": "10. NAIST", "last_name": "", "email": "nlp_annot_10@naist.ac.jp"}, "task": {"id": 138006, "data": {"ocr": "/lectrans/data/local-files/?d=/large/datas/frederikus-h/lectrans-testset/25.10.annot_tools/label-studio/ocr_check_storage_source/lec_slides/intmd_microeconomics/Dqko567cE9I/24.Dqko567cE9I-Scene-